          "desc": "Evaluate $g(0)$"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "State the $y$-intercept"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$g(0) = 5^0 - 5 = -4$. Therefore, the $y$-intercept is $-4$.",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "The $y$-intercept occurs where $x = 0$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Substitute $x = 0$ into $g(x) = 5^x - 5$.",
          "Evaluate $5^0 - 5 = 1 - 5 = -4$.",
          "Conclude that the $y$-intercept is $-4$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Thinking $5^0 = 0$ resulting in $-5$."
      }
    },
    {
      "subpart": "b",
      "stem": "the $x$-intercept is $1$.",
      "final_answer": "$1$",
      "mark_breakdown": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Evaluate $g(1)$ or solve $5^x - 5 = 0$"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "State the $x$-intercept"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$g(1) = 5^1 - 5 = 0$. Therefore, the $x$-intercept is $1$.",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "The $x$-intercept occurs where $g(x) = 0$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Set $5^x - 5 = 0$.",
          "Solve $5^x = 5^1$, which gives $x = 1$.",
          "Conclude the $x$-intercept is $1$."
